# Strata 8x16 text-mode font.
#
# An original design for the Strata machine's 80x30 text display. Compile with
# scripts/font.py (see its docstring for the format and the outputs).
#
# Metrics, in pixel rows 0-15 (top first) and columns 0-7 (left first):
#   cap height    10  rows 3-12 (also the ascender height of b d f h k l)
#   x-height       7  rows 6-12
#   baseline          row 12 is the lowest row of non-descending glyphs
#   descenders     3  rows 13-15 (g j p q y, and the tail of Q)
#   width             text glyphs use columns 0-6; column 7 stays blank so
#                     neighboring glyphs never touch
#
# Style: vertical stems are 2 pixels wide, horizontal strokes 1 pixel.
# Centered stems sit in columns 3-4, the middle of the cell. The zero is
# slashed; I has flat serifs top and bottom, l a top serif and a tail to the
# right, 1 a flag and a base.
#
# Graphics use CP437 code points. Single box lines are 1 pixel wide at column
# 3 and row 7; double lines are 1 pixel wide at columns 2 and 4 and rows 6 and
# 8, centered on the single lines so that the two families align. Box, block
# and shade glyphs reach the cell edges so they tile without gaps.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Symbols (CP437 0x01-0x1F)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

